★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
Spring Boot 4.0 broke its old monolithic `spring-boot-autoconfigure` / `spring-boot-test-autoconfigure` jars into one fine-grained module per feature, each living at `module/<artifactId>` in the `spring-projects/spring-boot` monorepo and each still publishing its own `-sources.jar`/`-javadoc.jar` to Maven Central under that artifact ID — so the URL template is mechanically derivable from the artifact name alone, which is why I could stay confident without hitting the network.
